\subsection{Decay of heavy quarks}

The decay modes of heavy quarks can be classified into two categories according to final state particles. One mode, named as gauge-boson mode, involves a new gauge boson and a SM quark. The other mode involves a 331 charged Higgs boson and a SM quark, named as charged Higgs mode. We take $T$ quark as an example to illustrate its decay branching ratio.

